  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Find the solutions **in radians** to the equation $4\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x-3=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Round your answers to **one decimal place**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x-3 & =0 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =3 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\frac{3}{4})=0.643\\,501\u2026\u22480.6\n$$\n\nSince $0.6$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=0.6.$\n\nTo generate solutions in the domain, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +0.643\\,501\u2026\u22483.8.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=0.6$ and $x=3.8.$",
